WEBVTT

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:47.910
I could probably get a room here.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:48.490
Yes, sir.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.080
We don't have so many American tourists like before.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.030
Now it is always refugees.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.410
Things have a way of changing.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:57.990
Can I send a cable from here?

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:58.630
Yes, sir.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.700
I will send.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:01.530
Thank you.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.780
About 10,000 miles from Philadelphia to Macau.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.920
In getting there, it gives a man a lot of time to think.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.280
You don't bother to answer any questions about yourself.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.900
Maybe because you figure you know all the answers.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.980
or maybe it's because you don't know the answers the real answers but you can't help wondering

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:42.410
about the others what brought them here what keeps them here what are they going to do to wind up with

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:50.560
before they leave with me it was simple what brought me here and thousand dollars what was

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:58.040
going to keep me here a woman only until i found her and what was i going to wind up with another

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.970
twenty thousand when i got up

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.030
Back to Philadelphia, city of brotherly love.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.400
Barney Pendleton's office.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.940
Barney Pendleton and the city of brotherly love.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:10.740
What a combination.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:16.360
Didn't say hello to you on a Sunday morning without making it sound like drop dead.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:29.270
Come in.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.880
A wire from Eddie Darrell.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.460
We were wrong about the day being in Hong Kong.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:37.820
She's in Macau.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.250
Barney, do you still think he'll be able to get her back here?

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.870
He's the only man in the world who can.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.370
She's in love with him.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.620
With him, she'd walk in front of trains.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.420
You ought to know that I'm not in the habit of tossing $30,000 into a game that I'm not sure of.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.060
Maybe, but you've already given him ten of it.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.900
And it might be worth it for him to keep that and stay over there.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:59.190
In case it turns out he's still in love with her.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.380
That's why I sent Cliff. There won't be any double-crossed.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:16.800
Friends, you're open news service?

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:17.460
Yes, sir.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.040
I wonder if you can give me a little information.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.900
I'm tracking down a story that broke out of your Hong Kong office about three weeks ago.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.580
That's right, sir.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.620
It had to do with a woman named Christine Lawrence.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.050
Do you know anything about it?

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.850
Christine Lawrence? Yes, I made you remember the story.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.020
I understand she's living in Macau, and I'm trying to locate her.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.700
Would you happen to have her address?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.860
My name is Darrow, Eddie Darrow, the Seattle Herald.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.900
I see. I'm sorry, Mr. Darrow, but I'm afraid we haven't too much on Miss Lawrence in our files.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.980
She's been seen on and off at the Lisbon Club. You might try down there.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.370
The Lisbon Club? Thank you very much.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:50.810
You're welcome.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.320
Thank you.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.000
