Yes. He and Danny own some Las Vegas property together.

00:46:16.680 --> 00:46:19.080
Danny's will left half to you, and Barney wants to buy it.

00:46:19.560 --> 00:46:21.500
But the deal's so involved, you'd have to be there.

00:46:22.140 --> 00:46:28.840
Eddie, Barney isn't worried about any property.

00:46:31.120 --> 00:46:34.300
He's worried about 20 pages of testimony that could put him behind bars for life.

00:46:37.230 --> 00:46:37.590
Testimony?

00:46:37.710 --> 00:46:40.350
What do I know about his and Danny's business transactions?

00:46:42.130 --> 00:46:46.860
I put it all down on paper after they tried to kill me and put it in a safety deposit box.

00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:51.360
If anything happens to me, the vault will be open in the presence of a federal officer.

00:46:52.830 --> 00:46:54.170
That's why Barney wants me back.

00:46:55.210 --> 00:46:56.630
To get that testimony if he can.

00:47:02.270 --> 00:47:03.720
I suck takin' me.

00:47:04.110 --> 00:47:05.770
We've got a lot stacked up against us.

00:47:06.930 --> 00:47:08.150
But everything's out in the open now.

00:47:08.290 --> 00:47:11.140
We're starting fresh and even like before.

00:47:11.700 --> 00:47:14.010
Before was such a long time ago.

00:47:14.850 --> 00:47:15.810
Oh, we'll make it up.

00:47:16.440 --> 00:47:17.360
Every minute of it.

00:47:17.460 --> 00:47:21.280
We just pack up and leave right now, this minute.

00:47:21.580 --> 00:47:23.930
That easy.

00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:26.300
Oh, we'll find the way, Chris.

00:48:28.190 --> 00:48:29.790
to be continued

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:36.210
getting breakfast? Mr. Keating, leave very early. Thank you, Willie.

00:49:04.636 --> 00:49:05.516
634, please.

00:49:09.660 --> 00:49:10.660
Hello, Eddie?

00:49:11.420 --> 00:49:11.720
Chris.

00:49:12.764 --> 00:49:13.524
Where are you phoning from?

00:49:13.788 --> 00:49:14.388
for my room.

00:49:15.452 --> 00:49:17.832
Eddie Justin's gone. He left my plane this morning.

00:49:18.684 --> 00:49:19.264
Are you sure?

00:49:20.092 --> 00:49:20.652
I'm positive.

00:49:21.596 --> 00:49:23.116
Already, this may be our only chance.

00:49:23.996 --> 00:49:25.196
He knows I was with you last night.

00:49:26.044 --> 00:49:27.004
He was waiting in the car.

00:49:28.284 --> 00:49:28.884
I'm waiting on the phone.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:31.020
Listen, Chris, don't get panicky.

00:49:31.140 --> 00:49:33.500
You'll have to stick close to the house under any condition.

00:49:35.590 --> 00:49:36.270
Justin has it.

00:49:36.410 --> 00:49:38.380
I'll stop making other arrangements.

00:49:38.620 --> 00:49:40.420
I'll call you just as soon as I make some headway.

00:49:40.460 --> 00:49:41.780
Be careful around Willie.

00:49:41.880 --> 00:49:42.640
Don't show any signs.

00:49:42.880 --> 00:49:43.980
I won't.

00:49:45.830 --> 00:49:46.330
Goodbye, Eddie.

00:49:46.470 --> 00:49:50.440
Uh, 739, please.

00:49:50.620 --> 00:49:51.360
Airport, main desk.

00:49:51.480 --> 00:49:51.840
Flight information?

00:49:52.320 --> 00:49:52.480
Yes.

00:49:52.800 --> 00:49:54.980
Uh, I'd like to get in touch with a Mr. Justin Keat.

00:49:55.040 --> 00:49:56.940
Can you tell me if his plane is already left?

00:49:57.140 --> 00:49:57.380
Yes, sir.

00:49:58.350 --> 00:49:58.550
It has.

00:49:58.690 --> 00:49:59.250
Thank you.

00:50:06.660 --> 00:50:11.420
Try to phone you at your hotel. What are you doing here at this time of the day?

00:50:11.960 --> 00:50:13.900
I thought I'd come in early to rehearse some new music.

00:50:14.100 --> 00:50:16.000
My repertoire is getting positively monotonous.

00:50:16.810 --> 00:50:19.710
Ellen, how good of a friend are you?

00:50:20.340 --> 00:50:22.700
That depends on how you evaluate the quality of friendship.

00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:25.640
I wouldn't lend you money because borrowing destroys friendship,

00:50:26.360 --> 00:50:29.460
but I would consider it a privilege if you would let me help you get her out of Macau.

00:50:30.320 --> 00:50:30.760
Then you know.

00:50:30.900 --> 00:50:35.440
If our friendship, which for your sake I hope will soon be terminated, were to continue,

00:50:35.600 --> 00:50:38.990
you will discover there is very little about Macau that I do not know.

00:50:39.170 --> 00:50:40.810
How do I do it, Alan?

00:50:41.110 --> 00:50:42.070
Transportation, papers.

00:50:42.270 --> 00:50:43.580
We don't care where we go.

00:50:45.440 --> 00:50:48.920
If at four o'clock this afternoon, you will go to the Rue Casa Drue Cadrau,

00:50:49.020 --> 00:50:51.800
you will find a tailor shop owned by my good friend Joy Tart.

00:50:52.220 --> 00:50:54.640
He's an excellent tailor with documents as well as cloth.

00:50:55.120 --> 00:50:56.040
Everything will be arranged.

00:50:56.360 --> 00:50:59.250
I don't know how to thank you.

00:50:59.510 --> 00:50:59.970
This is no...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:02.440
Time for thanks. You'd only flounder into speechlessness.

00:51:02.844 --> 00:51:04.104
But it would be wise to be cautious.

00:51:04.604 --> 00:51:05.284
You might be followed.

00:51:06.108 --> 00:51:08.068
Now go home, my friend, and spend the day with your dreams.

00:52:00.090 --> 00:52:01.070
Oh, yes, Mr. Darrell.

00:52:01.760 --> 00:52:02.740
Your shirts are finished.

00:52:03.130 --> 00:52:04.970
I think you'll like it very much.

00:52:05.430 --> 00:52:06.590
Fine as can't tell itself.

00:52:07.200 --> 00:52:07.760
Very rare.

00:52:09.490 --> 00:52:10.670
Ellen's a very good friend.

00:52:10.950 --> 00:52:13.090
Everything necessary for the trip is in here,

00:52:13.340 --> 00:52:15.860
including instruction to place and friends

00:52:15.860 --> 00:52:17.300
should you need help on the way.

00:52:17.490 --> 00:52:19.510
Most important, your passport and the ladies.

00:52:19.810 --> 00:52:20.170
Thanks.

00:52:20.660 --> 00:52:21.360
I send you a bill.

00:52:21.580 --> 00:52:22.420
Goodbye, Mr. Darrell.

00:52:22.840 --> 00:52:23.140
Goodbye.

00:52:24.150 --> 00:52:24.610
Good luck.

00:52:47.210 --> 00:52:57.800
Talk, all set. We leave tomorrow at 1. First by junk, then seaplane to Bombay, and then from there, Australia by boat.

00:52:58.250 --> 00:52:58.950
Oh, anyplace.

00:53:00.190 --> 00:53:02.900
Any place in the world, just so it's away from here.

00:53:03.380 --> 00:53:04.620
We'll meet at my place at 11.

00:53:05.280 --> 00:53:08.020
Tell Willie you're going shopping and don't bring anything with you except what you're wearing.

00:53:08.510 --> 00:53:10.490
I'm in his office. I'd better get downstairs. Good night, darling.

00:53:11.110 --> 00:53:12.450
Remember, 11 sharp.

00:53:26.350 --> 00:53:26.530
Willie.

00:53:26.750 --> 00:53:27.450
Yes, Miss Lawrence.

00:53:27.850 --> 00:53:29.910
I'm going shopping for a while this afternoon.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:31.640
so don't bother to fix lunch for me.

00:53:31.760 --> 00:53:32.380
Thank you, Miss Lawrence.

00:54:00.320 --> 00:54:02.200
What's wrong, Eddie? You look as though you'd seen a ghost.

00:54:03.510 --> 00:54:04.470
I thought you were away.

00:54:05.360 --> 00:54:07.980
Now, how did you know that? I told no one I was leaving Macau.

00:54:08.820 --> 00:54:11.780
I just thought you were. I didn't see you at the club last night.

00:54:12.890 --> 00:54:14.870
I approve much more of your manners at the club.

00:54:15.070 --> 00:54:16.270
Aren't you going to invite us in?

00:54:17.100 --> 00:54:17.620
Oh, sure.

00:54:23.870 --> 00:54:27.220
In fact, I've been away. Just returned. Sooner than I expected.

00:54:28.920 --> 00:54:29.980
I called Chris, but she wasn't...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:31.780
at home. I thought you might know where she is.

00:54:32.540 --> 00:54:34.380
Look, Justin, if you've got something on your mind,

00:54:34.460 --> 00:54:36.740
let's get it off, huh? I'd much rather have a drink

00:54:36.740 --> 00:54:39.900
if you don't mind. Just remember that I haven't

00:54:39.900 --> 00:54:41.640
any soda. It won't take but a minute to get some.

00:54:41.760 --> 00:54:43.900
Plain water will do nicely. No trouble. I prefer

00:54:43.900 --> 00:54:44.800
plain water.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:00.340
Thank you.

00:55:30.190 --> 00:55:31.880
Oh, it's a tremality.

00:55:32.920 --> 00:55:33.620
I'm very flattered.

00:55:33.860 --> 00:55:34.980
Something I learned from you.

00:55:35.560 --> 00:55:37.800
Fancy service can cover a lot of third-rate liquor.

00:55:39.010 --> 00:55:41.240
Sam, cheers.

00:55:41.560 --> 00:55:47.580
I think somebody knocked.

00:55:48.300 --> 00:55:49.640
Probably the guy from down the hall.

00:55:49.880 --> 00:55:50.400
Real pest.

00:55:50.670 --> 00:55:51.470
Talks my ear off.

00:55:51.610 --> 00:55:53.370
Sam, be a good fellow and get rid of the pest.

00:55:53.490 --> 00:55:54.010
Never mind.

00:55:55.100 --> 00:55:55.760
I'll do it myself.

00:55:58.740 --> 00:55:59.480
How's the boy, Eddie?

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:02.020
Oh, I didn't know you had visitors. How are you?

00:56:02.380 --> 00:56:04.080
My name's Chalmer, Cliff Chalmer.

00:56:04.820 --> 00:56:07.840
Look, I hate to bust up the party, kid, but it's 11 o'clock.

00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:12.290
What a guy. You make a date for 11, you're lucky if you see him at 12.

00:56:12.530 --> 00:56:13.790
Got a memory like a corpse.

00:56:14.120 --> 00:56:15.760
Forgot all about it. Do we still have time?

00:56:16.020 --> 00:56:17.220
Yeah, if you gotta move on.

00:56:17.730 --> 00:56:18.770
I hate to run out on you.

00:56:18.770 --> 00:56:20.870
Forget it. Where are you going?

00:56:21.130 --> 00:56:24.030
Oh, didn't Eddie tell you we got a big stack on us 6th at Happy Valley?

00:56:24.330 --> 00:56:25.990
No, I'm not a racing man myself.

00:56:26.170 --> 00:56:28.690
I never thought of asking Eddie about a gamble like that.

00:56:30.220 --> 00:56:31.100
Well, we'll move along.

00:56:36.890 --> 00:56:37.610
Good day, Eddie.

00:56:45.920 --> 00:56:48.370
Mrs. Pavilion, I've seen you around the Lisbon club.

00:56:48.510 --> 00:56:49.070
I've been there.

00:56:49.600 --> 00:56:52.920
I figured it might get a little crowded if we all arrived at the same time.

00:56:53.170 --> 00:56:54.790
First Keith, then me, then a dame.

00:56:54.970 --> 00:56:56.900
So, I told the lady you had company.

00:56:57.040 --> 00:56:58.500
She's tucked away in a room downstairs.

00:57:00.980 --> 00:57:02.220
Maybe this will clear it up.

00:57:02.820 --> 00:57:05.580
Sit down.

00:57:09.860 --> 00:57:12.420
The idea was to take her back to the States, not to Australia.

00:57:12.950 --> 00:57:14.090
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:57:14.210 --> 00:57:16.190
Listen, Buster, maybe we can't touch the dame,

00:57:16.270 --> 00:57:17.930
but you're not so immune, you know what I mean?

00:57:18.640 --> 00:57:20.360
Pendleton has a thing about being cross.

00:57:20.560 --> 00:57:21.700
Makes him real peevish.

00:57:22.020 --> 00:57:23.720
He's got 30 grand tied up in you.

00:57:24.370 --> 00:57:25.570
Now you get what I'm driving at?

00:57:28.120 --> 00:57:29.500
I'm beginning to get the whole picture.

00:57:31.190 --> 00:57:50.620
This much for Barney Pendleton.

00:57:51.160 --> 00:57:53.300
He at least picked a tale with some brains and imagination.

00:57:54.060 --> 00:57:56.060
Don't romance me, Darryl. I'm married.

00:57:56.650 --> 00:57:57.550
You didn't let me finish.

00:57:58.030 --> 00:57:59.970
You said you were smart, but you know Phi Beta...

00:58:00.030 --> 00:58:03.190
Kappa, took a lot of trouble to set this dame up.

00:58:03.650 --> 00:58:06.470
Well, now she's right, and I don't want you around messing things up.

00:58:07.010 --> 00:58:10.470
She'll go anywhere I say, anywhere, but back to the States.

00:58:10.650 --> 00:58:11.850
Anywhere don't pay off.

00:58:13.200 --> 00:58:14.640
This girl's no fool, Charmer.

00:58:15.110 --> 00:58:17.030
She knew Bonnie wanted her, and she knew why.

00:58:17.870 --> 00:58:18.630
So what are you proving?

00:58:19.180 --> 00:58:21.700
So I had to find a way to win her over, gain her confidence.

00:58:22.080 --> 00:58:25.720
Well, I did it, with a confession that brought tears to her eyes.

00:58:26.540 --> 00:58:28.020
I told her why I was here.

00:58:28.220 --> 00:58:29.600
This I'm not interested in.

00:58:31.760 --> 00:58:34.400
All I know is you got visas for all the wrong places

00:58:34.400 --> 00:58:36.420
and the name of a boat that sails for Australia.

00:58:36.700 --> 00:58:39.360
Look, once I get her out of here, she'll follow me to the moon on a bike.

00:58:39.820 --> 00:58:43.030
But in the meantime, suppose she decides to check me out

00:58:43.030 --> 00:58:44.470
and find there's no boat for Australia.

00:58:44.840 --> 00:58:47.140
Then she knows I've been giving her a line and then we're dead.

00:58:49.290 --> 00:58:51.190
Okay, so now you're in Bombay. Now what?

00:58:51.380 --> 00:58:53.820
Now I tell her something went wrong, that the Elgin isn't sailing,

00:58:53.920 --> 00:58:55.620
the skipper got cold feet, anything.

00:58:56.430 --> 00:58:59.980
But I tell her there's another ship, the Dauphin, crummy little...

00:59:00.030 --> 00:59:05.690
I made a deal with the captain, only we have to board her 20 minutes before she sails, at night,

00:59:05.960 --> 00:59:08.300
when no one's around to ask any questions. Catch?

00:59:08.580 --> 00:59:09.080
Keep talking.

00:59:09.300 --> 00:59:11.400
Then I take Chris down in the stateroom and I keep her there.

00:59:11.960 --> 00:59:15.580
By the time she finds out, we're headed for the States. We're two days out at sea.

00:59:16.180 --> 00:59:17.960
What is she gonna do? Jump overboard?

00:59:19.590 --> 00:59:22.610
I don't know. It still smells like soft-boiled fish.

00:59:22.770 --> 00:59:24.790
It's that kind of a job and it's the only way it'll work.

00:59:25.360 --> 00:59:26.660
Of course, if you've got a better notion.

00:59:28.180 --> 00:59:29.980
No, I'll let you work yours up.

00:59:30.060 --> 00:59:33.870
Only remember, I'll be watching.

00:59:35.960 --> 00:59:37.140
Come on, let's go talk to her.

00:59:38.830 --> 00:59:47.330
They must have found her.

00:59:47.490 --> 00:59:49.010
Not unless she wandered out of here.

01:00:20.870 --> 01:00:21.910
No, she go away.

01:00:22.110 --> 01:00:23.010
Well, didn't she come back?

01:00:23.250 --> 01:00:25.640
Oh, yes, she come back. Go away again with Mr. Keats.

01:00:26.090 --> 01:00:26.550
Where'd they go?

01:00:26.850 --> 01:00:28.500
They go to boat. They come back tonight.

01:00:28.820 --> 01:00:29.740
Did they say where they were going?

01:00:30.030 --> 01:00:33.140
Oh, no. Very nice day. Maybe they go only for a ride.

01:00:33.220 --> 01:00:34.620
Yeah, it's a great day, all right.

01:00:44.420 --> 01:00:44.680
Damn.

01:00:47.240 --> 01:00:48.000
It's a man with you.

01:00:48.140 --> 01:00:48.780
Where's Keat?

01:00:49.100 --> 01:00:49.720
He's out.

01:00:51.170 --> 01:00:52.310
He's out. Where is he?

01:00:53.780 --> 01:00:56.820
Well, right now I'd say he's sneaking up on a short honeymoon.

01:00:57.170 --> 01:00:59.830
He and that Lawrence dame. I mean, Miss Lawrence.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:08.780
are getting married in Hong Kong this afternoon. Eddie, what's the matter? Don't you believe in

01:01:08.780 --> 01:01:09.080
marriage?

01:01:59.660 --> 01:01:59.980
that I've seen.

01:02:00.030 --> 01:02:02.430
Justin, beauty like that was meant to be shared.

01:02:02.570 --> 01:02:04.630
Would I put the Mona Lisa under wraps if I owned it?

01:02:05.220 --> 01:02:07.560
No, as a matter of fact, I'd rather enjoy showing croissants.

01:02:08.040 --> 01:02:09.880
Really, Justin, she's your wife,

01:02:10.180 --> 01:02:12.260
not some painting you've added to your collection.

01:02:13.180 --> 01:02:13.820
Excuse me.

01:02:14.150 --> 01:02:28.730
Really, I'm a brother.

01:02:28.970 --> 01:02:29.970
Oh, of course not, old man.

01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:36.590
that wonderful girl your sister well look who's here what a pity you weren't invited

01:02:36.590 --> 01:02:41.300
every time i called on the phone they said you were out so i had to do it this way i gotta talk

01:02:41.300 --> 01:02:46.280
to you chris i'm not going anyplace with you so help me chris you don't come with me i'll break up

01:02:46.280 --> 01:02:59.980
the place enough isn't it why did you do it chris you were going to talk well go ahead

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:03.390
Start with the story about the girl who'd follow you to the moon on a bicycle.

01:03:04.020 --> 01:03:06.660
Or maybe you'd prefer the story about the girl who had to jump off a ship in mid-ocean.

01:03:07.360 --> 01:03:09.040
Chris, no. You've got to listen to me.

01:03:09.510 --> 01:03:11.250
Pendleton had a tale on me, and I didn't know it.

01:03:11.630 --> 01:03:14.250
He found out about our plans for Australia. I had to feed him a line.

01:03:14.350 --> 01:03:16.330
Oh, you lied prettier when you were setting me up.

01:03:16.920 --> 01:03:18.840
Well, I'm set up now where you can't touch me.

01:03:18.920 --> 01:03:20.140
Chris, you've got to believe me.

01:03:23.610 --> 01:03:25.890
I had to convince this charmer that I wasn't crossing Barney.

01:03:26.460 --> 01:03:27.460
That's what you heard.

01:03:28.330 --> 01:03:29.970
And I'm sure he's convinced like I...

01:03:33.620 --> 01:03:37.410
I guess I haven't got the right to ask you to believe me, and it's one of those things I couldn't prove.

01:03:38.740 --> 01:03:43.590
But I feel sorry for you, Chris, because you're going to wonder about this for a long, long time.

01:04:15.100 --> 01:04:17.160
was a very foolish thing to do. She's his wife

01:04:17.160 --> 01:04:19.290
now. Yes, I know. To take his wife

01:04:19.290 --> 01:04:21.210
like that in the midst of his friends was worse than

01:04:21.210 --> 01:04:23.720
striking him. I'm afraid you've declared open war.

01:04:23.760 --> 01:04:25.900
That's all right with me. He's a very

01:04:25.900 --> 01:04:28.430
dangerous man. I know he is, but I've got a few

01:04:28.430 --> 01:04:29.310
things working for me.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.720
Maybe enough to link him with the illegal traffic the papers have hinted at.

01:04:35.760 --> 01:04:36.900
You overestimate yourself.

01:04:37.890 --> 01:04:38.230
Maybe.

01:04:38.760 --> 01:04:41.440
But you know as well as I that Hanfire that got knocked over that night,

01:04:41.650 --> 01:04:43.270
he didn't get money from Keith as a gift.

01:04:43.520 --> 01:04:44.480
He sold him something.

01:04:45.550 --> 01:04:48.730
Do you think that he would hesitate for one instant to use Miss Lawrence to stop you?

01:04:48.930 --> 01:04:49.590
No, my friend.

01:04:49.710 --> 01:04:51.090
He has the strongest weapon of all.

01:04:51.400 --> 01:04:52.260
Your love for her.

01:04:52.740 --> 01:04:54.540
Threaten her and you'll do anything he asks.

01:04:55.480 --> 01:04:57.120
But there's got to be a way to stop him.

01:04:57.570 --> 01:04:58.410
Kill him then, my friend.

01:04:58.570 --> 01:04:59.970
And immediately turn yourself over to...

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:04.410
to the police for safety that way you can at least enjoy a victory until you are executed

01:05:04.410 --> 01:05:28.490
don't be surprised if i give it a try you better not be seen with me anymore good night you should

01:05:28.490 --> 01:05:29.790
do something about the crummy

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:36.640
they got on these doors this ship you were telling me about the dolphin i've been checking

01:05:36.640 --> 01:05:40.600
and there ain't none you could have made a deal for how can you check it you can't even spell it

01:05:40.940 --> 01:05:47.170
look darrow don't get cute now you look charmer the show's over she married keat what are you

01:05:47.170 --> 01:05:51.540
giving me now it's straight i didn't believe it either till they came back from hong kong

01:05:51.540 --> 01:05:53.270
I thought you had this sewed up.

01:05:54.090 --> 01:05:58.070
I did, until she heard us talking in here.

01:06:06.110 --> 01:06:07.450
Okay, so she's married. Now what?

01:06:08.380 --> 01:06:10.920
Barney will have to figure a new angle. There's nothing more I can do.

01:06:11.890 --> 01:06:16.220
I'm sick of the whole mess. Where are you going?

01:06:16.910 --> 01:06:19.570
Get a cable off to Barney. Find out how to handle this.

01:06:45.130 --> 01:06:52.150
reception alone without me i tell you i don't enjoy being made a fool of i don't either didn't

01:06:52.150 --> 01:06:58.080
ask him to come you're in love with him aren't you i hate it don't lie to me about a man who

01:06:58.080 --> 01:06:59.980
traveled six thousand miles to take me back to bonn

01:07:01.250 --> 01:07:02.630
Now ask me if I love him.

01:07:03.180 --> 01:07:06.440
Being married for revenge is no more flattering than being made a fool.

01:07:08.200 --> 01:07:10.400
I have a few plans for this man you hate.

01:07:13.300 --> 01:07:13.700
Justin!

01:07:36.330 --> 01:07:37.230
In the library, Sam.

01:07:37.510 --> 01:07:44.190
I couldn't figure out a better wedding present for you, Mac.

01:07:44.730 --> 01:07:45.170
Now, wait a minute.

01:07:46.330 --> 01:07:47.350
You're Eddie Darrow's friend.

01:07:47.790 --> 01:07:48.290
What do you want?

01:07:48.680 --> 01:07:50.520
Your widow has to go back to the States.

01:07:50.990 --> 01:07:52.810
This was supposed to go so nobody got hurt,

01:07:52.850 --> 01:07:54.090
and I'm sorry they have to do this,

01:07:54.170 --> 01:07:55.350
but you know how these things go.

01:07:57.100 --> 01:07:58.400
Eddie decides to get selfish

01:07:58.400 --> 01:07:59.980
and take her with him to Australia for...

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:00.480
himself.

01:08:00.860 --> 01:08:02.120
Then you get into the act.

01:08:03.388 --> 01:08:06.108
This proves you should never trust people, not even yourself.

01:08:06.748 --> 01:08:07.948
Drop it in front of you.

01:08:17.244 --> 01:08:18.244
them.

01:08:30.508 --> 01:08:33.108
Go to the club and pick up Leon. I want you to get rid of Darrow.

01:08:33.328 --> 01:08:35.328
You

01:09:07.100 --> 01:09:10.910
I just didn't want you to be alarmed there someone tried to break in I think

01:09:10.910 --> 01:09:13.370
it'll be better if we leave the house until after the police have been here

01:09:15.260 --> 01:09:23.590
you ain't here for me

01:10:02.300 --> 01:10:02.800
Chris!

01:10:05.852 --> 01:10:07.012
Eddie, we've got to get out of here.

01:10:07.644 --> 01:10:07.884
Oui.

01:10:08.892 --> 01:10:10.052
That man I heard you talking to.

01:10:10.908 --> 01:10:12.168
He's dead. Justin killed him.

01:10:12.700 --> 01:10:13.200
Charmers?

01:10:13.692 --> 01:10:15.572
Yes, he came to the house to kill Justin.

01:10:15.644 --> 01:10:17.644
Somehow Sam got behind him and made him drop the gun.

01:10:18.268 --> 01:10:19.688
When he turned around, Justin shot it.

01:10:20.284 --> 01:10:22.044
I heard Justin tell Sam to get Leon.

01:10:22.524 --> 01:10:24.684
He's using Chalmers as an excuse to have you killed.

01:10:27.132 --> 01:10:27.972
I've got it yet.

01:10:28.540 --> 01:10:29.660
We'll have to take our chance.

01:10:30.410 --> 01:10:33.250
You don't understand. It isn't just Sam and Leon. It's Justin. He'll stop at nothing.

01:10:33.720 --> 01:10:39.890
Kristen, are you there?

01:10:40.030 --> 01:10:41.920
I have to leave.

01:10:42.080 --> 01:10:44.280
Sam and Leon, it's Lawrence.

01:10:45.440 --> 01:10:45.880
Then you know.

01:10:46.050 --> 01:10:46.390
Yes.

01:10:46.610 --> 01:10:48.030
I'll make him understand that we must leave.

01:10:48.420 --> 01:10:49.180
He wants to stay?

01:10:49.300 --> 01:10:50.280
There's no sense running away.

01:10:51.060 --> 01:10:52.260
You never beat him in Macau.

01:10:52.620 --> 01:10:53.400
Listen, my friend.

01:10:53.460 --> 01:10:55.860
At times, there's a thin line between courage and stupidity.

01:10:56.060 --> 01:10:57.060
This is one of those times.

01:10:57.200 --> 01:10:58.220
What would you gain here?

01:10:58.300 --> 01:10:59.700
To save your face and lose your life?

01:11:00.700 --> 01:11:03.540
What about her? Haven't you caused her enough unhappiness?

01:11:04.170 --> 01:11:06.610
You have the choice between trying to live by taking her away

01:11:06.610 --> 01:11:09.160
or certainly dying so that Mr. Keat could have her again.

01:11:09.630 --> 01:11:11.050
That would be pleasant for her, wouldn't it?

01:11:12.130 --> 01:11:13.110
You're always right, Alan.

01:11:13.470 --> 01:11:15.830
We have no time. Sam and Leon are on the way from the club.

01:12:32.300 --> 01:12:33.520
It's the only way they could get out of here.

01:12:34.092 --> 01:12:36.252
Come on, we'll get down to the docks and pick up Leon on the way.

01:12:37.964 --> 01:12:38.884
All right, Ella, where to?

01:12:39.596 --> 01:12:41.616
Mr. Keats boat first, then I hope Kowloon.

01:12:41.932 --> 01:12:43.212
But Alan, he'll find us in Calhoun.

01:12:43.252 --> 01:12:45.072
What about that plane of Bombay? What about Australia?

01:12:45.580 --> 01:12:46.580
That plan was for a scheme.

01:12:46.924 --> 01:12:48.344
I had hoped that now you'd be for victory.

01:12:49.900 --> 01:12:50.860
What are you driving at?

01:12:51.244 --> 01:12:52.264
Leave the man to Macau.

01:12:52.652 --> 01:12:55.772
Since the shooting the night you arrived, the police have learned much more than he realizes.

01:12:56.204 --> 01:12:59.044
If you're smart, you can wreck his organization where the worst damage is done.

01:12:59.276 --> 01:12:59.996
in your own country.

01:13:00.890 --> 01:13:02.110
You sure picked the right people, Alan.

01:13:02.620 --> 01:13:05.140
If we go back to the States, we're in as big a jam as we are here.

01:13:05.760 --> 01:13:08.540
Eddie, if we get out of this, I'm through running.

01:13:09.190 --> 01:13:10.510
I want us to go home where we belong.

01:13:11.690 --> 01:13:12.310
All right, Chris.

01:13:12.970 --> 01:13:14.830
We'll get everything cleared up with Barney once and for all.

01:13:17.000 --> 01:13:18.200
All right, Alan, what's the plan?

01:13:19.200 --> 01:13:20.970
Kowloon, Prince of Wales dock, birth 12.

01:13:21.320 --> 01:13:23.580
There's a ship, the SS Malabar, bound for San Francisco.

01:13:24.060 --> 01:13:24.820
It will leave tomorrow.

01:13:25.220 --> 01:13:27.400
It's still loading, so except for a guard, the crew is ashore.

01:13:27.920 --> 01:13:28.640
Stow away on it.

01:13:28.870 --> 01:13:29.970
And when you're at sea, announce yourself...

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:31.990
to the first officer. He's a friend of mine.

01:13:32.130 --> 01:13:35.490
You seem to have friends in all the right places.

01:13:38.570 --> 01:13:40.860
What's this? A list of names and addresses.

01:13:41.100 --> 01:13:43.280
The men and women who received Mr. Keats' contraband

01:13:43.280 --> 01:13:44.480
in all the port cities of America.

01:13:45.090 --> 01:13:47.430
Perhaps with it, you too can win some friends in the right places.

01:13:47.610 --> 01:13:49.400
You play good piano, Alan,

01:13:49.500 --> 01:13:51.480
but I'm trying to figure out what you really are.

01:13:51.620 --> 01:13:53.120
I thought you knew.

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:29.980
Thank you.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:59.980
Thank you.

01:16:02.340 --> 01:16:27.260
see the captain sorry nobody's a lot of board come back there and you go forward outside i'll be right

01:16:27.260 --> 01:16:27.400
up

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:31.620
up there with him. Stay on the starboard side.

01:17:30.250 --> 01:17:59.970
The light of magic.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:00.580
wouldn't be seen.

01:18:00.660 --> 01:18:01.160
They'll match.

01:18:01.360 --> 01:18:02.440
This grain dust is worse

01:18:02.440 --> 01:18:03.120
than dynamite.

01:19:45.040 --> 01:19:45.340
Chris?

01:21:51.050 --> 01:21:56.460
left after the explosion, but we fished his bag out of the wreckage. Dean Lawrence Maynard,

01:21:56.910 --> 01:21:58.890
321-0 South Elm, Philadelphia.

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:01.580
States. Too bad.

01:22:01.780 --> 01:22:03.940
Wonder what she was doing on a freighter like that.

01:22:04.530 --> 01:22:06.670
Well, we'd better send it over to the American consulate.

01:22:06.900 --> 01:22:08.520
They'll have to cable her family, you know.

01:22:09.720 --> 01:22:10.780
We'll do it right away.

01:22:40.140 --> 01:22:52.880
Kennedy's office please. Issue a warrant for Barney Pendleton. That's right. I've got enough to put him and his syndicate away for a thousand years. I'll be down and get it. I want to pick this monkey up personally.

01:23:05.180 --> 01:23:05.860
What are you thinking about?

01:23:09.590 --> 01:23:11.870
How nice it would be if we could just stop the clock in this ship.

01:23:12.790 --> 01:23:14.210
Spend the rest of our lives right here.

01:23:14.820 --> 01:23:16.060
We've got a few more weeks.

01:23:16.900 --> 01:23:17.500
A few weeks.

01:23:18.330 --> 01:23:19.590
Maybe our whole lifetime, Eddie.

01:23:19.890 --> 01:23:22.960
The closer we get, the more frightened I am.

01:23:23.940 --> 01:23:24.380
I don't know.

01:23:24.950 --> 01:23:26.210
Maybe it's the moonlight affecting you.

01:23:27.030 --> 01:23:28.250
But I've got a gambler's hunch.

01:23:28.940 --> 01:23:29.860
The kind you go broke on.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:37.540
get rich quick. I've got a feeling everything is going to turn out all right. Your hunch is good enough for me, darling.
